IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-rules`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- the questions of the PRINCIPAL: the person who makes, or has made, an enduring
-- power of attorney, here typically someone injured whose injury may take away, or has taken away, their decision
-- making capacity, and whose claim, damages or compensation an attorney may run, settle, receive and manage.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the Act is applied to. "Can I make an enduring power of attorney?", "Who can be my attorney?",
-- "Was it signed and witnessed properly?", "Can my attorney settle my injury claim now?", "Is my power still in force?",
-- "May my attorney buy a house with my damages and put it in both our names?", "Can I be compensated for my attorney's
-- breach, and by when?", "Can I ask VCAT, and by when for a rehearing?". Where a family member asks for the person (as
-- nearest relative, or for the estate after death), the questions are still worded from the principal's seat. The
-- attorney's own questions are in poa-seat-attorney.l4. VCAT, the Supreme Court and the Public Advocate get no seat:
-- their satisfaction, orders and determinations are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of poa-rules.l4.
-- The two deadline rules (ss 79, 133) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Powers of
-- Attorney Act 2014, Version No. 007 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 2014: the questions of the principal`

§§ `Decision making capacity and my nearest relative`

@export Do I have decision making capacity for this matter (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 4, 5)? You are presumed to have it unless there is evidence to the contrary; otherwise you have it if, with any practicable and appropriate support, you can understand, retain, use or weigh the information and communicate the decision. Capacity is matter by matter and may be temporary; it must be assessed at the time and place you can show it best.
GIVEN `evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is any evidence that you may not have capacity for this decision (a decision with a high risk of seriously harming your health or wellbeing may, with other factors, be such evidence)
      `appearance only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that doubt rests only on your appearance, or only on a decision others think unwise
      `understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can understand the information relevant to the decision and its effect, if it is explained in a way suited to you (simple language, visual aids or other means)
      `retain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can retain that information long enough to make the decision
      `weigh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can use or weigh that information in making the decision
      `communicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can communicate the decision and your views and needs in some way (speech, gesture or other means), with any support you need
GIVETH A `Whether I have decision making capacity`
`Do I have decision making capacity` MEANS
    `s 4 -- my decision making capacity` `evidence` `appearance only` `understand` `retain` `weigh` `communicate`

@export Who is my nearest relative (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 3)? The first relative aged 18 or over in this order: spouse or domestic partner; child; parent or step-parent; sibling or step-sibling; grandparent; grandchild; uncle or aunt; nephew or niece; the eldest within a group. Your nearest relative may apply to VCAT about your power (s 122), apply for compensation (s 78), and is told when an attorney's appointment ends while you lack capacity and no other attorney can be told (s 54).
GIVEN `partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or domestic partner aged 18 or over
      `child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a child aged 18 or over
      `parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a living parent or step-parent aged 18 or over
      `sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister aged 18 or over (including one adopted by your parent)
      `grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a living grandparent
      `grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a grandchild aged 18 or over
      `uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an uncle or aunt aged 18 or over
      `nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a nephew or niece aged 18 or over
GIVETH A `My nearest relative`
`Who is my nearest relative` MEANS
    `s 3 -- my nearest relative` `partner` `child` `parent` `sibling` `grandparent` `grandchild` `uncle or aunt` `nephew or niece`

§§ `Making an enduring power of attorney`

@export Can I make an enduring power of attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 23)? Only if you are 18 or over and have decision making capacity to make it, which includes understanding the conditions you may set, when it starts, that your attorney will then have your powers, that you can revoke it while you have capacity, that it continues if you lose capacity, and that without capacity you cannot oversee it.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is any evidence that you may not have capacity to make the power
      `appearance only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that doubt rests only on your appearance, or only on a decision others think unwise
      `understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can understand what the power does: the conditions you may set, when it starts, that your attorney then has your powers, that you can revoke it while capable, that it continues if you lose capacity, and that you then cannot oversee it
      `retain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can retain that information long enough to decide
      `weigh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can use or weigh that information in deciding
      `communicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can communicate your decision in some way, with any support you need
GIVETH A `Whether I can make an enduring power of attorney`
`Can I make an enduring power of attorney` MEANS
    `s 23 -- whether I can make an enduring power of attorney` `age` (`s 4 -- my decision making capacity` `evidence` `appearance only` `understand` `retain` `weigh` `communicate`)

@export Can I give my attorney this power in an enduring power of attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22, 26)? You may authorise anything you can lawfully do by an attorney, including running, settling and receiving the money from your injury claim (a financial matter), but not making your will, voting, consenting to marriage, decisions about your children, managing your estate after death, or an unlawful act. Medical treatment decisions are made under the Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016 instead.
GIVEN `power` IS A `Kind of power to give` @desc The power: running, settling or defending a legal claim for you and receiving the money; managing your money, property and compensation; deciding where and with whom you live and other personal matters; medical treatment decisions; making or revoking your will; making or revoking an enduring power of attorney for you; voting; consenting to your marriage or sexual relationship or its dissolution; decisions about your child's care or adoption; a surrogacy arrangement or substitute parentage order; managing your estate after death; consenting to an unlawful act; something else you can lawfully do by an attorney; or something you cannot lawfully do by an attorney
GIVETH A `Whether I can give this power`
`Can I give my attorney this power` MEANS
    `ss 22, 26 -- whether I can give this power` `power`

@export Can this person or body be my attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22(4), 28)? An individual aged 18 or over who is not an insolvent under administration and not your paid care worker, health provider or accommodation provider; for financial matters, someone convicted of a dishonesty offence only if they told you and it is recorded in the power. A trustee company only for financial matters; the Public Advocate only for personal matters. A family member on a government carer payment is not a care worker.
GIVEN `attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc Who the proposed attorney is: an individual; a trustee company; the Public Advocate, as attorney; or another body corporate
      `matters` IS A `Matters the attorney is for` @desc What they would be attorney for: for personal matters only; for financial matters only (including your injury claim); or for both personal and financial matters
      `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc Their age in whole years (any number for a company or the Public Advocate)
      `insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are an insolvent under administration (an undischarged bankrupt, or under a personal insolvency agreement or arrangement not yet complete)
      `dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have been convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty punishable by at least 3 months' imprisonment, anywhere
      `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether they told you and the disclosure is recorded in the power (answer no otherwise)
      `paid to care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are paid, from any source (including your compensation), for services caring for you
      `carer payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they receive a carer payment or other government benefit for providing home care for you
      `health provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they provide health care to you in the practice of a profession or in the course of business
      `accommodation provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they are, professionally or administratively, responsible for or involved in providing your accommodation
      `winding up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trustee company: whether a proceeding to wind it up has commenced (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A `Whether this person is eligible to be my attorney`
`Can this person be my attorney` MEANS
    `s 28 -- whether this person is eligible to be my attorney` `attorney` `matters` `their age` `insolvent` `dishonesty` `disclosed` (`s 3 -- this person is my care worker` `paid to care` `carer payment` `health provider`) `health provider` `accommodation provider` `winding up`

@export Was my enduring power of attorney, or my instrument revoking it, signed and witnessed as the Act requires (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 5A, 32-36, 45-49)? It must be in the prescribed form, signed by you or by an eligible adult at your direction and in your presence, and witnessed by two eligible adults (not an attorney, the signer, a relative of yours or of an attorney, or your care worker or accommodation provider), one of them authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner, who sign, date and certify it in your and each other's presence. Remote witnessing by audio visual link is allowed on the same day in Victoria with a special witness signing last. If not, only VCAT can decide it is valid anyway (s 117).
GIVEN `instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument` @desc Which document: an enduring power of attorney; or an instrument of revocation
      `prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in (or to the effect of) the prescribed form
      `signed myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed it yourself (rather than someone signing at your direction)
      `signer age` IS A NUMBER @desc If someone signed for you: their age in whole years (any number if you signed)
      `signer witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether they were also a witness (answer no if you signed)
      `signer attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If someone signed for you: whether they are an attorney under the power (answer no if you signed)
      `w1 age` IS A NUMBER @desc The first witness's age in whole years
      `w1 attorney or signer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first witness is an attorney under the power, or the person who signed for you
      `w1 relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first witness is your relative or an attorney's relative (spouse or domestic partner, child, parent or step-parent, sibling or step-sibling, grandparent, grandchild, uncle or aunt, nephew or niece)
      `w1 carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first witness is your paid care worker or your accommodation provider
      `w2 age` IS A NUMBER @desc The second witness's age in whole years
      `w2 attorney or signer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second witness is an attorney under the power, or the person who signed for you
      `w2 relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second witness is your relative or an attorney's relative
      `w2 carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second witness is your paid care worker or your accommodation provider
      `qualified witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one witness is authorised to witness affidavits (such as a lawyer or justice of the peace) or is a medical practitioner
      `witnessed together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both witnesses were present and saw the signing, and signed and dated it in your presence and each other's (presence may be by audio visual link under remote witnessing)
      `certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each witness certified that you appeared to sign (or direct the signing) freely and voluntarily and appeared to have capacity, stated they are not an excluded person, stated their qualification if relied on, and signed the certificate
      `remote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the remote witnessing procedure (audio visual link) was used
      `same day in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If remote: whether every step was done on the same day and within Victoria (answer yes otherwise)
      `special witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If remote: whether one witness was a special witness (an Australian lawyer, a justice of the peace, or a prescribed person) who signed last and certified the procedure (answer yes otherwise)
GIVETH A `Whether the instrument was executed as the Act requires`
`Was my instrument signed and witnessed properly` MEANS
    `ss 32-36, 45-49, 5A -- whether the instrument was executed as the Act requires` `instrument` `prescribed form` `signed myself`
        (`ss 34, 47 -- the person signing for me is eligible` `signer age` `signer witness` `signer attorney`)
        (`ss 35(2), 48(2) -- the witness is eligible` `w1 age` `w1 attorney or signer` `w1 relative` `w1 carer`)
        (`ss 35(2), 48(2) -- the witness is eligible` `w2 age` `w2 attorney or signer` `w2 relative` `w2 carer`)
        `qualified witness` `witnessed together` `certified` `remote` `same day in Victoria` `special witness`

@export Is my enduring power of attorney effective as to this attorney, who has accepted it (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 37, 38)? Only if the attorney signed a statement of acceptance in the prescribed form, witnessed by an adult who also signed (not needed for a trustee company), stating that they are eligible, understand an attorney's obligations and the consequences of breaking them, and undertake to comply; an alternative attorney also states they understand when they may act and are prepared to act.
GIVEN `alternative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is an alternative attorney
      `trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney is a trustee company
      `signed acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they signed a statement of acceptance in the prescribed form in the power
      `witnessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult witnessed their signing and signed that they did (answer yes for a trustee company)
      `statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement says they are eligible, understand an attorney's obligations and the consequences of failing them, and undertake to act under the Act
      `alternative statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an alternative attorney: whether it also says they understand when they may act and are prepared to act in the attorney's place (answer yes otherwise)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my power effective as to this attorney` MEANS
    `ss 37, 38 -- my power is effective as to this attorney` `alternative` `trustee company` `signed acceptance` `witnessed` `statements` `alternative statements`

@export How must my attorneys act together if I appointed more than one (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 30)? Joint attorneys (the default if you did not say) all act and sign together; several attorneys may each act alone; joint and several attorneys either way; majority attorneys by a majority; unless your power provides otherwise.
GIVEN `appointment` IS A `How my attorneys were appointed` @desc How the power appoints them: jointly; severally; jointly and severally; by majority; or it does not say
      `otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power sets out some other way for them to act
GIVETH A `How my attorneys must act`
`How must my attorneys act together` MEANS
    `s 30 -- how my attorneys must act` `appointment` `otherwise`

§§ `When my attorney may act`

@export May my attorney act for me now on this matter (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22(2), 39, 41, 42, 83)? From the making of the power unless you specified a later time; whatever you specified, while you lack capacity for the matter; and, once your attorney has begun acting because you lacked capacity, even after you regain it. If VCAT has made an administration order (money) or guardianship order (personal matters) for you, only so far as VCAT authorises. You may still act yourself. Assumes the power is in force (see the question on whether it has ended).
GIVEN `scope` IS A `What my power covers` @desc What your power covers: personal matters only; financial matters only; both; matters you specified, including this one; or matters you specified, not including this one
      `matter` IS A `Kind of matter` @desc The matter: a financial matter (money, property, or a legal matter about them, such as your injury claim); a personal matter (where you live, daily life, or a legal matter about them); or medical treatment
      `start` IS A `When I said my power begins` @desc When your power says it begins: nothing specified; immediately; when you cease to have decision making capacity for the matter; or another time, circumstance or occasion
      `time come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you specified another time, circumstance or occasion: whether it has come (answer no otherwise)
      `lack capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now lack decision making capacity for this matter
      `began acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney has already begun acting for this matter because you lacked capacity for it
      `administration order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made an administration order for you under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019
      `guardianship order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made a guardianship order for you under that Act
      `VCAT authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is such an order: whether VCAT has authorised your attorney to act despite it (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may act now`
`May my attorney act for me now` MEANS
    `ss 22, 39, 41, 83 -- whether my attorney may act now` `scope` `matter` `start` `time come` `lack capacity` `began acting` `administration order` `guardianship order` `VCAT authorised`

@export May my attorney bring, settle or defend my injury or compensation claim and receive the money for me now (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 3, 22(2), 39, 41, 83)? A claim and the money from it are a financial matter (a legal matter about your financial affairs, and receiving money payable to you), so your power must cover financial matters (or name the claim) and be exercisable; if VCAT has made an administration order for you, your attorney may act only so far as VCAT authorises.
GIVEN `scope` IS A `What my power covers` @desc What your power covers: personal matters only; financial matters only; both; matters you specified, including this claim; or matters you specified, not including it
      `start` IS A `When I said my power begins` @desc When your power says it begins: nothing specified; immediately; when you cease to have decision making capacity for the matter; or another time, circumstance or occasion
      `time come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you specified another time, circumstance or occasion: whether it has come (answer no otherwise)
      `lack capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now lack decision making capacity to run or settle the claim
      `began acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney has already begun acting on your financial matters because you lacked capacity
      `administration order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made an administration order for you (for example after a court ordered your damages paid to an administrator or State Trustees)
      `VCAT authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether VCAT has authorised your attorney to act for your financial matters (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may act now`
`May my attorney run or settle my claim now` MEANS
    `ss 22, 39, 41, 83 -- whether my attorney may act now` `scope` `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)` `start` `time come` `lack capacity` `began acting` `administration order` FALSE `VCAT authorised`

@export May my alternative attorney act in my attorney's place (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 31(2))? In the circumstances your power specifies; if it specifies none, when the attorney dies, loses capacity for the matters, is not willing or able to act, or has their appointment revoked under s 54 (insolvency, becoming your paid carer, health or accommodation provider, a dishonesty conviction).
GIVEN `specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power specifies when the alternative attorney may act
      `arisen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether those circumstances have arisen (answer no otherwise)
      `died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney has died
      `lost capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney no longer has decision making capacity for the matters
      `unwilling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney is otherwise not willing or able to act
      `revoked s 54` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attorney's appointment was revoked under s 54 (insolvency, becoming your paid carer, health or accommodation provider, or a dishonesty conviction for a financial attorney)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May my alternative attorney act` MEANS
    `s 31(2) -- my alternative attorney may act` `specified` `arisen` `died` `lost capacity` `unwilling` `revoked s 54`

§§ `When my power ends`

@export Is my enduring power of attorney still in force as to this attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 43, 44, 51-56, 59, 119, 120)? It ends on your death, by its own terms, by your valid revocation, by a later enduring power (unless it says otherwise), or by VCAT; and as to one attorney when they die, lose capacity, resign, or after appointment become insolvent, your paid carer, health or accommodation provider, or (for money matters) are convicted of dishonesty. Losing your own capacity does not end it (s 22(3)).
GIVEN `by its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power's own terms have ended it
      `I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (asked for your estate)
      `declared invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has declared the power invalid
      `I revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you revoked the power, or this attorney's appointment, by a valid instrument of revocation
      `later power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a later enduring power of attorney that does not say this one continues
      `VCAT revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT revoked the power, or this attorney's appointment
      `attorney died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this attorney has died
      `attorney lost capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this attorney no longer has decision making capacity for the matters the power covers
      `disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an individual attorney: whether, after appointment, they became an insolvent under administration, your paid care worker, health provider or accommodation provider, or (if for financial matters) were convicted or found guilty of a dishonesty offence
      `company wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trustee company attorney: whether it was wound up or ceased to be registered after appointment
      `resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this attorney has validly resigned
      `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has suspended the power for a period that is still running
GIVETH A `Whether my power is in force as to this attorney`
`Is my power still in force` MEANS
    `Part 5 -- whether my power is in force as to this attorney` `by its terms` `I died` `declared invalid` `I revoked` `later power` `VCAT revoked` `attorney died` `attorney lost capacity` `disqualified` `company wound up` `resigned` `suspended`

@export Can I revoke my enduring power of attorney, or one attorney's appointment (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 44-50)? Yes, if you have decision making capacity to make an enduring power giving the same power; by an instrument of revocation in the prescribed form, signed and witnessed like the power itself. You must take reasonable steps to tell your attorneys, but not telling them does not undo the revocation.
GIVEN `evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is any evidence that you may not have capacity to make an enduring power giving the same power
      `appearance only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that doubt rests only on your appearance, or only on a decision others think unwise
      `understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can understand what such a power does and what revoking it means, explained in a way suited to you
      `retain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can retain that information long enough to decide
      `weigh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can use or weigh that information in deciding
      `communicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can communicate your decision in some way, with any support you need
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I revoke my power` MEANS
    `s 44 -- I may revoke my power` (`s 4 -- my decision making capacity` `evidence` `appearance only` `understand` `retain` `weigh` `communicate`)

§§ `My attorney's dealings with my money (only if my attorney is acting)`

@export May my attorney enter into a transaction in which their own interests (or a relative's, business associate's or close friend's) may conflict with their duty to me, such as using my damages to buy property in both our names (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 64, 65)? Not unless you authorised it beforehand, VCAT authorised it, or it is validated (by you while you have capacity, or by VCAT once completed). Permitted gifts and maintenance, dealing with property you already hold jointly, and buying jointly while you have capacity are outside the duty.
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney is an attorney for financial matters
      `conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is or may be a conflict between their duty to you and the interests of the attorney or their relative, business associate or close friend
      `exception` IS A `Exception the transaction falls under` @desc Whether it is: no exception; a gift made under s 67; maintenance of your dependant under s 68; dealing with property you and your attorney hold jointly (or a loan or guarantee for it); or acquiring property to be held jointly with your attorney (or a loan or guarantee for it)
      `capacity then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had decision making capacity for the matter when the transaction was entered into
      `I authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you authorised, before it, this transaction, this kind of transaction, or conflict transactions generally
      `VCAT authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT authorised it, or the kind, or conflict transactions generally, before it
      `completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transaction has been completed
      `I validated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you validated it afterwards at a time you had decision making capacity for it
      `VCAT validated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT validated the completed transaction
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may enter into the transaction`
`May my attorney enter into this conflict transaction` MEANS
    `ss 64, 65 -- whether my attorney may enter into the transaction` `financial attorney` `conflict` `exception` `capacity then` `I authorised` `VCAT authorised` `completed` `I validated` `VCAT validated`

@export May my attorney give away my property or money as a gift (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 67)? Only an attorney for financial matters, only if your power does not forbid it, the gift is reasonable given your finances, and it is either a seasonal or special-event gift to your relative or close friend, or a donation of a kind you made or might be expected to make. It may go to the attorney or their family.
GIVEN `financial attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney is an attorney for financial matters
      `forbidden` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a condition or restriction in your power forbids or limits this gift
      `reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is reasonable given all the circumstances, in particular your financial circumstances
      `seasonal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is to your relative or close friend and of a seasonal nature or for a special event (such as a birth or marriage)
      `donation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a type of donation you made while you had capacity, or might reasonably be expected to make
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my attorney make this gift` MEANS
    `s 67(1) -- my attorney may make the gift` `financial attorney` `forbidden` `reasonable` `seasonal` `donation`

@export Is my attorney entitled to be paid for acting (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 70)? Not unless your power specifically authorises it or the law does. Your attorney also must not use the position for profit (s 63(1)(c)).
GIVEN `power authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power specifically authorises paying the attorney
      `law authorises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether some law authorises it (for example a trustee company's statutory fees)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my attorney entitled to be paid` MEANS
    `s 70 -- the attorney is entitled to be paid` `power authorises` `law authorises`

@export What happens if my personal matters attorney and my financial matters attorney disagree (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 71, 72)? The personal matters attorney's decision prevails and the financial matters attorney must implement it, unless (for several attorneys) your power or VCAT says otherwise; but if implementing it would seriously deplete your finances, the financial attorney must apply to VCAT instead. Either may apply to VCAT.
GIVEN `several` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorneys act severally and each has authority for the matter
      `otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your power, or a VCAT order, says how such a disagreement is resolved
      `depletion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether implementing the personal matters decision would seriously deplete your financial resources
GIVETH A `What happens when my attorneys disagree`
`What happens when my attorneys disagree` MEANS
    `ss 71, 72 -- what happens when my attorneys disagree` `several` `otherwise` `depletion`

§§ `Compensation from my attorney (only if I suffered a loss through their breach)`

@export Can my attorney be ordered to compensate me for a loss they caused (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 73-77)? The Supreme Court or VCAT may order it for a loss caused by their contravening the Act while acting as attorney, even if they were convicted, the power was invalid or revoked, or you have died (then to your estate). Not where they acted on the Court's or VCAT's advice or order, or relied in good faith on a power they did not know was invalid or revoked; and not for any part they are relieved of because they acted honestly and reasonably.
GIVEN `contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss was caused by your attorney contravening the Act's enduring power provisions (for example a conflict transaction, an unauthorised gift, mixing your money with theirs, poor records) while acting as attorney
      `court advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they acted in compliance with advice, a direction or an order of the Supreme Court or VCAT, without knowingly misleading it
      `invalid or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the power was invalid or had been revoked when they acted
      `good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether they acted in good faith without knowing, or having reason to believe, that it was invalid or revoked (answer no otherwise)
      `relief` IS A `Relief from liability` @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved them of their personal liability: no relief; relieved of part; or relieved of all
      `died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (the question is then asked for your estate)
GIVETH A `Whether I can be compensated`
`Can I be compensated by my attorney` MEANS
    `ss 73-77 -- whether I can be compensated` `contravention` `court advice` `invalid or revoked` `good faith` `relief` `died`

@export Can this person apply for compensation from my attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 78)? You, any attorney under your power, the executor or administrator of your estate, the Public Advocate, your nearest relative, or anyone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in your affairs.
GIVEN `applicant` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who is applying: you; an attorney under your power; the executor or administrator of your estate; the Public Advocate; your nearest relative; someone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in your affairs; or someone else
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply for compensation` MEANS
    `s 78 -- this person may apply for compensation` `applicant`

@export By when must an application for compensation from my attorney be made (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 79)? Within 6 months after your death, or your attorney's, or the first of the two deaths; the Supreme Court or VCAT may extend the time. While you and your attorney are both alive the Act sets no time limit (no answer).
GIVEN `I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (asked for your estate)
      `my death` IS A DATE @desc The day you died (any date if not)
      `they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney has died
      `their death` IS A DATE @desc The day they died (any date if not)
      `extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has extended the time
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if not extended)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I apply for compensation` MEANS
    `s 79 -- the last day to apply for compensation from` (`s 79(1) -- the day of the first death` `I died` `my death` `they died` `their death`) `extended` `extended to`

@export Is the application for compensation from my attorney in time (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 79)? It must be made within 6 months after the first relevant death (yours or your attorney's), or within any longer time the Supreme Court or VCAT allows; while both are alive the Act sets no limit.
GIVEN `I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (asked for your estate)
      `my death` IS A DATE @desc The day you died (any date if not)
      `they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your attorney has died
      `their death` IS A DATE @desc The day they died (any date if not)
      `extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has extended the time
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if not extended)
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been made
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day it was made (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Is my compensation application in time` MEANS
    `s 79 -- where my compensation application stands` (`s 79(1) -- the day of the first death` `I died` `my death` `they died` `their death`) `extended` `extended to` `applied` `applied on` `today`

§§ `VCAT and my power (only if someone goes to VCAT about it)`

@export Can this person apply to VCAT for an order about my enduring power of attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 116, 122)? You, any attorney, the Public Advocate, your nearest relative, or anyone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in your affairs. VCAT may then decide the power's scope, its exercise, its validity, a transaction's validity, and order accounts lodged and audited.
GIVEN `applicant` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who is applying: you; an attorney under your power; the executor or administrator of your estate; the Public Advocate; your nearest relative; someone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in your affairs; or someone else
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply to VCAT about my power` MEANS
    `s 122 -- this person may apply to VCAT about my power` `applicant`

@export May VCAT declare my enduring power of attorney invalid (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 118, 119)? Only if satisfied that you lacked capacity to make it, it did not comply with the Act when made, dishonesty or undue influence was used on you, or it was otherwise legally invalid. If declared invalid it is void from the start.
GIVEN `lacked capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied you lacked decision making capacity to make it when it was made
      `did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied it did not comply with the Act's requirements when made
      `undue influence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied dishonesty or undue influence was used on you to make it
      `otherwise invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied it was legally invalid for some other reason when entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May VCAT declare my power invalid` MEANS
    `s 118 -- VCAT may declare my power invalid` `lacked capacity` `did not comply` `undue influence` `otherwise invalid`

@export May VCAT treat my enduring power of attorney, or my revocation of it, as valid although it was not signed or witnessed as the Act requires (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 116(1)(b), 117)? Only if VCAT is satisfied that it was intended to have that effect (by you and, for a power, the attorney), that you had capacity when it was signed, and that you signed it, or directed and watched someone sign it, freely and voluntarily.
GIVEN `intended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied it was intended as an enduring power of attorney (by you and the attorney) or as a revocation (by you)
      `capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied you had decision making capacity (to make the power, or one giving the same power) when it was signed
      `freely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied you signed it freely and voluntarily, or freely and voluntarily directed the person who signed for you and were present
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May VCAT treat my instrument as valid` MEANS
    `s 117 -- VCAT may treat my defectively executed instrument as valid` `intended` `capacity` `freely`

@export May VCAT revoke my attorney's appointment (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 120(2))? Only if VCAT is satisfied that your attorney is not complying with the Act and that you lack capacity to make an enduring power giving the same power (while you have it, you can revoke the appointment yourself). VCAT may also revoke, vary or suspend the power itself (s 120(1)).
GIVEN `not complying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied your attorney is not complying with the Act's enduring power provisions
      `lack capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied you lack decision making capacity to make an enduring power of attorney giving the same power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May VCAT revoke my attorney's appointment` MEANS
    `s 120(2) -- VCAT may revoke my attorney's appointment` `not complying` `lack capacity`

@export Can a rehearing be sought of VCAT's order about my enduring power of attorney (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) ss 124-133)? A party (you and every attorney are parties) may apply, as may the Public Advocate; someone given notice but not a party, or with a special interest and no notice, needs VCAT's leave. There is no rehearing of an order suspending the power, of an order made by VCAT's President, or of a rehearing or leave application. Applying does not stop the order operating unless VCAT stays it.
GIVEN `standing` IS A `The applicant's standing` @desc The applicant: a party to the first hearing (you always are); given notice but not a party; not given notice but with a special interest in your affairs; the Public Advocate, as applicant; or none of these
      `suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order suspended the enduring power of attorney
      `President` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT was constituted by its President (with or without others)
      `rehearing application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order was itself on an application for a rehearing or for leave
GIVETH A `Whether a rehearing can be sought`
`Can a rehearing be sought` MEANS
    `ss 126, 130 -- whether a rehearing can be sought` `standing` `suspension` `President` `rehearing application`

@export By when must an application for a rehearing, or for leave, of VCAT's order about my power be made (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 133)? Within 28 days after the day of the order; if VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then asked for written reasons, from the day the written reasons were given. The Act gives no power to extend.
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the order
      `written reasons requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then requested written reasons
      `reasons given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given (any date if none were requested)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for a rehearing` MEANS
    `the date` 28 `days after` (`s 133(2) -- the day of the order` `made on` `written reasons requested` `reasons given on`)

@export Is the application for a rehearing, or for leave, of VCAT's order about my power in time (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 133)? It must be made within 28 days after the day of the order (or of the written reasons, if requested after oral reasons).
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the order
      `written reasons requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then requested written reasons
      `reasons given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given (any date if none were requested)
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been made
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day it was made (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Is my rehearing application in time` MEANS
    `s 133 -- where my rehearing application stands` (`s 133(2) -- the day of the order` `made on` `written reasons requested` `reasons given on`) `applied` `applied on` `today`

§§ `Offences against me (only if someone acted dishonestly)`

@export What is the maximum penalty for dishonestly obtaining my enduring power of attorney or its revocation, or for my attorney dishonestly using it, to gain money or cause me loss (Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) s 135)? 5 years' imprisonment or 600 penalty units or both; a company, 2400 penalty units. It applies even if the power was invalid or revoked. The answer is in penalty units; 0 years means no imprisonment.
GIVEN `company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (a company)
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`What is the maximum penalty for dishonest dealing with my power` MEANS
    `s 135 -- the maximum penalty` `company`
